@startuml signal-correlation
title US-06: Signal Correlation - Proximity candidate triggers supersession of existing SIGNAL_LOSS

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nproximity.candidates" as ProxKafka
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
database "Redis\nalert-state:{id}\n(hash)" as AlertState
database "Redis\nrecent-loss:{id}\n(hash)" as RecentLoss
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

note over Evaluator
  Runs on Kafka consume from proximity.candidates.
  Only the elected leader evaluates.
  SIGNAL_LOSS is already emitted immediately on detection.
  If proximity arrives within the correlation window,
  the SIGNAL_LOSS is superseded — not suppressed.
end note

ProxKafka -> Evaluator : consume proximity.candidates event\n{ pair_key, entity_a_id, entity_b_id,\n  episode_start_ms, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, distance_at_detection }

note over Evaluator
  Proximity candidate: unscheduled pair detected
  by the Correlation Worker.
  Known associates already filtered upstream.
  Check each entity for an active or recent signal loss.
end note

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:{entity_a_id}
AlertState --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id } or nil

Evaluator -> AlertState : HGETALL alert-state:{entity_b_id}
AlertState --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id } or nil

alt active signal loss on entity A or B (alert-state present)
  note over Evaluator
    Entity is currently dark. alert-state hash provides:
    - dark_since_ms: start of the signal loss window
    - signal_loss_alert_id: ID of the emitted SIGNAL_LOSS alert to supersede
  end note
else no active signal loss - check recent-loss window
  Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:{entity_a_id}
  RecentLoss --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id } or nil (TTL = COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS)

  Evaluator -> RecentLoss : HGETALL recent-loss:{entity_b_id}
  RecentLoss --> Evaluator : { dark_since_ms, signal_loss_alert_id } or nil

  note over RecentLoss
    Entity resumed broadcasting but was dark recently.
    Position Consumer wrote recent-loss before deleting alert-state.
    Still eligible for composite if within COMPOSITE_CORRELATION_WINDOW_MS.
  end note
end

alt dark_since_ms found and episode_start_ms within loss window
  Evaluator -> Neo4j : MATCH (a)-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT {\n  idempotency_key: $pair_key+':'+$episode_start_ms\n}]->(b)\nRETURN e
  Neo4j --> Evaluator : edge context { episode_start_ms, distance_at_detection }

  note over Evaluator
    Both signals confirmed.
    Supersede the SIGNAL_LOSS and emit COMPOSITE.
    See composite-emission diagram for the atomic transaction.
  end note

  Evaluator -> Evaluator : -> atomic supersession transaction\n(composite-emission diagram)
end

@enduml
